    "q-157254": {
      "dom_id": "step-q157254",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.",
      "worked_solution": "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
